' purpose: bounded offline ELF64 program/dynamic metadata without loader or filesystem access
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/elf-metadata.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/elf-metadata.test.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/elf-requirements.test.mjs
' context: _spec/_plans/ml-runtime-redesign.md section 30 owns historical v1; section 33 owns current v2 qualification work.
' status: inspectElf64 preserves v1; inspectElf64Requirements adds bounded v2 declarations.
' rendering: retain house include; approved pinned local theme is substituted in renderer input only.
@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Offline ELF metadata — bounded program/dynamic metadata, no loader or reader
left to right direction

actor "Synthetic caller" as CALLER <<host>>
component "elf-metadata.mjs\ninspectElf64" as INSPECT <<app>>
component "Strict lower-only limits\nprivate bounded snapshot" as SNAPSHOT <<app>>
component "ELF64 little-endian x86-64\nheader / program headers" as HEADERS <<app>>
component "PT_DYNAMIC / DT_STRTAB\nunambiguous file-backed mapping" as DYNAMIC <<app>>
component "Bounded UTF-8 strings\nunresolved metadata" as STRINGS <<app>>
component "Optional requirements-v2\nversions / GNU notes / properties" as REQUIREMENTS <<app>>
component "Deeply frozen metadata\ninputSha256 / false assurance flags" as RESULT <<app>>
component "ElfMetadataError\nfixed code, no partial result" as ERROR <<error>>

CALLER ARROW_MAIN INSPECT : inspectElf64(bytes, tightened limits)
INSPECT ARROW_MAIN SNAPSHOT : validate native view, backing and cap before copy
SNAPSHOT ARROW_MAIN HEADERS : private bytes only; all U64 arithmetic in BigInt
HEADERS ARROW_MAIN DYNAMIC : validated spans and bounded declared slot count
DYNAMIC ARROW_MAIN STRINGS : unique string table; offsets stay inside captured bytes
STRINGS ARROW_MAIN RESULT : bounded UTF-8 JSON before publication
STRINGS ARROW_OPTIONAL REQUIREMENTS : inspectElf64Requirements only; v1 stays unchanged
REQUIREMENTS ARROW_MAIN RESULT : bounded declarations, not actual symbol/CPU proof
RESULT ARROW_MAIN CALLER : immutable plain data; no input-backed views

SNAPSHOT ARROW_ERROR ERROR : invalid backing/profile or exceeded cap
HEADERS ARROW_ERROR ERROR : unsupported format, overflow or malformed span
DYNAMIC ARROW_ERROR ERROR : duplicate singleton, missing DT_NULL or ambiguous mapping
STRINGS ARROW_ERROR ERROR : missing bounded NUL, invalid UTF-8/control or output overrun
REQUIREMENTS ARROW_ERROR ERROR : bad chains, overlaps, notes or property bounds
ERROR ARROW_ERROR CALLER : throw fixed failure; no partial-success metadata

note bottom of SNAPSHOT
v1 input<=1MiB; no unsafe backing memory
Program headers<=128; dynamic slots<=1024
Limits accept own data only and may tighten only
No filesystem/network/process/adapter callback
end note

note bottom of HEADERS
ELF64 / little-endian / machine62 / version1
ET_EXEC or ET_DYN; header64 / entry56
Reject extended program-header numbering
Convert file offsets after BigInt bounds checks
end note

note bottom of DYNAMIC
At most one PT_INTERP and one PT_DYNAMIC
First DT_NULL ends active-tag interpretation
Declared-slot cap includes unused tail slots
One entire file-backed PT_LOAD mapping only
Reject aliases, split spans and BSS-only data
end note

note bottom of STRINGS
Table<=64KiB; dynamic string<=1024 bytes with NUL
Interpreter<=256 bytes with NUL; DT_NEEDED<=32
Keep NEEDED order/duplicates and raw RPATH/RUNPATH
No path joins, search, expansion or dereference
end note

note bottom of RESULT
v1 JSON<=64KiB; digest is not provenance
Execution/decoder/loader/NoPython flags:false
Native/installed/Rust/training flags:false
No candidate or SDK archive read by this module
end note

note bottom of REQUIREMENTS
v2 input<=4MiB; output<=128KiB
Version records<=512; auxiliaries<=1024
Unique note bytes<=64KiB; notes<=128
Build ID<=64 bytes; property payload<=4096
No symbol, CPU, provenance or enforcement proof
end note

legend bottom
  Synthetic tests establish only this supported metadata subset, not actual candidate compatibility.
  Interpreter/library strings remain untrusted data and never become host-file allowances.
  v1 unknown tags remain opaque; v2 decodes bounded version and GNU-note declarations only.
  No relocations, actual symbol resolution, CPU detection or loader execution occurs.
  Source caps do not establish native heap, CPU, runtime-closure or F9/game authority.
  Source/version/provenance, real ELF dependency closure and decoder execution remain separate gates.
endlegend
@enduml
